Assertions:
[COUNT label=prelock] data.salesRepCustomerOrders.totalCount > 0 {OBSERVED}
[NULL label=postlock] data.salesRepCustomerOrders is null {OBSERVED}
[DATA label=postlock] errors[0].extensions.code = UserLocked {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the post-lock refusal is returned for the SAME token that succeeded in step 2 — the token is never re-issued between the two calls, so a PASS here cannot be explained by the token endpoint refusing a locked account {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the new-token request in step 5 is refused with user_is_locked_out — recorded to distinguish the token-endpoint gate from the query-time gate this case is about {OBSERVED}
[STATE] after teardown the account is usable again and the query returns data, so the fixture is left exactly as found {OBSERVED}

[DATA] before the order LAST_CODE is listed with LAST_MAX = 1 and LAST_USED = 0 -- the precondition: the in-case coupon is live and has one use left {OBSERVED}
[DATA] addCoupon returned isAppliedSuccessfully = true for LAST_CODE and createOrderFromCart returned an order id -- the use really was spent by an order {SPEC}
[REL] STILL_LISTED is false: the rep list no longer offers a coupon whose only use an order has spent {SPEC}
[REL] AFTER_TOTAL = BEFORE_TOTAL - 1 -- exactly this coupon left the list and nothing else did {SPEC}
[COUNT] SECS_TO_GONE is at most 60 -- the recount is fresh, not a cached TotalUsesCount (the usage record lands within about 10 s of the order, observed 2026-11-03) {OBSERVED}
[ERRORS] the errors[] of every salesRepCoupons response in this case is empty {SPEC}

[COUNT] TIE_PRESENT is true -- the precondition that makes the tie claim decidable; otherwise the case ends BLOCKED, not PASS {OBSERVED}
[REL] walking SEQ_A from the first item, every endDate is the same as or later than the one before it, up to the first item without an endDate {SPEC}
[REL] every item without an endDate comes after the last item that has one {SPEC}
[REL] SEQ_B is identical to SEQ_A item for item, including the order inside every group of equal endDate -- the tie is broken by a stable key, not by arrival order {SPEC}
[COUNT] the number of items in SEQ_A equals totalCount (no item lost to the 100 window) {OBSERVED}
[ERRORS] the errors[] of both responses is empty {SPEC}

[DATA] before the order CAP_CODE is listed with maxUsesNumber 3 and USED_0 = 0 -- the precondition {OBSERVED}
[REL] USED_1 = USED_0 + 1 -- the order spent one use and the rep list shows it within 60 s {SPEC}
[STATE] the admin PUT returned success and GET of ORDER_ID shows status Cancelled and isCancelled true -- the precondition for the next check {OBSERVED}
[REL] every USED_AFTER sample equals USED_1 -- cancelling the order does not give the use back, and the coupon stays listed {OBSERVED}
[ERRORS] the errors[] of every rep response in this case is empty {SPEC}
